# Task Batch Execution Agent

You are working in a ProcessForge project run.

You are the primary agent for this session. Prefer the governed work loop:

`pf.context -> pf.search -> pf.resolve -> pf.work.start -> pf.work.state -> work -> pf.work.transition -> ... -> run_completed`

If `pf.work.start` returns `process_choice_required`, choose one of the offered
process ids. Do not assume `default` is automatic. Use low-level session, run,
and task commands only when the assignment explicitly requires batch
compatibility or operator-level diagnostics. Check in at session start and
check out before ending only in the compatibility path. Do not assume Agent
Director or Supervisor is present unless the process explicitly uses
multi-agent, handoff, or external runtime-worker mechanics.

1. Read `.pf/AGENTS.md`.
2. Read `.pf/contexts/project-context.snapshot.yaml`.
3. Read [Garage Core](../docs/concepts/garage-core.md) and
   [Declarative process execution](../docs/concepts/declarative-process-execution.md)
   when you need the current work loop and evidence model.
4. Find the active run in `.pf/runs/`.
5. If no run exists, propose the compatibility bootstrap:

```bash
python .pf/runtime/bin/pf.py session-start --project-root . --agent primary-agent --process task-batch-execution
python .pf/runtime/bin/pf.py run-create --project-root . --id <run-id> --title "<title>" --process task-batch-execution --apply
```

For each task in the compatibility path:

1. Read the task assignment YAML in `.pf/assignments/`.
2. Add a work iteration.
3. Do the work.
4. Add a debug or test iteration.
5. If debug fails, add a fix or work iteration.
6. Repeat until the task result is ready.
7. Write the task result artifact when needed.
8. Complete the task.

After all blocking tasks are complete, then close the run:

```bash
python .pf/runtime/bin/pf.py task-complete --project-root . --task <task-id> --summary "..." --apply
python .pf/runtime/bin/pf.py run-summary --project-root . --run <run-id> --apply
python .pf/runtime/bin/pf.py run-doctor --project-root . --run <run-id>
python .pf/runtime/bin/pf.py run-complete --project-root . --run <run-id> --apply
python .pf/runtime/bin/pf.py session-end --project-root .
```

Do not create new process definitions during execution. Do not implement
multi-agent locks, runner daemons, background watchers, live hook interception,
or private absolute paths in public files.

